.remember/

# Claude Code — shared config is committed, per-developer overrides are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# codebase-index is machine-local (pip install + init). Shared Claude config
# under .claude/ stays tracked; only the indexer install is ignored.
.claude/cache/codebase-index/
.claude/skills/codebase-index/
.codeindexignore
.mcp.json

# .NET — the solution described in docs/backend-architecture/ lands here.
#
# artifacts/ is where every build writes, per Directory.Build.props's Output
# group: one directory at the root rather than a bin/ and an obj/ beside every
# project file. The bin/ and obj/ rules below are no longer what keeps output
# out of a commit — they are what keeps a checkout that predates that change
# from committing what it already has on disk.
#
# The leading slash is the whole of the pattern's reach. Without it git matches
# the name at every depth, so a source directory somebody called artifacts/
# would go untracked without a word — and §4.1 puts generated output at the
# root and nowhere else. The rules below take the depth deliberately, because a
# checkout predating the move has those directories beside each project.
/artifacts/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
.vs/
.idea/
*.received.*

# Local configuration and secrets — never commit these.
appsettings.*.local.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.p12

# Python — the licence gate in .github/licence-gate/ is a script, not a package.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Helm — `helm dependency update` resolves deploy/helm/*/Chart.yaml's file://
# entries by PACKAGING the sibling chart into charts/ and writing a digest into
# Chart.lock. Neither is source: the tarball is a binary copy of a directory two
# levels up, and the lock pins nothing a remote repository could move, because
# nothing here comes from one.
#
# Chart.lock earns its place when a dependency is fetched over the network and
# a build has to be reproducible against a repository that changed. Committed
# here it would be a second copy of the version already in Chart.yaml, and one
# that goes stale on a bump — which is the drift CLAUDE.md's one rule exists to
# close. `helm dependency update` is the whole of the setup, and smoke.sh and
# the CI job both run it before anything else.
deploy/helm/*/charts/
deploy/helm/*/Chart.lock
